WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.680
The Arrowverse contains a vast wealth of heroes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.640
But every shining knight has a weakness. These&nbsp;
are the weaknesses of the Arrowverse's best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.480
and brightest, from their debilitating&nbsp;
phobias to their reckless attitudes.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.240
Beth Chapel just wants to belong. While she loves&nbsp;
her parents, she also resents them a little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.560
as they stopped paying much attention to her&nbsp;
once she grew old enough to take care of herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.520
As a result, this young genius gloms onto&nbsp;
Courtney Whitmore and Yolanda Montez when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.040
realizes they're forming some kind of secret club.&nbsp;
Upon learning they're superheroes, she gets even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.320
more excited. Once Courtney realizes that Beth&nbsp;
has somehow managed to activate Dr. Mid-Nite's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.840
artificial intelligence goggles, she allows her to&nbsp;
join the new Justice Society. However, her clingy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:49.120
nature and desperate desire to prove herself&nbsp;
leads her to make mistakes and act impulsively.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.560
Rick Tyler was raised by his uncle Matt.&nbsp;
Unbeknownst to him, his father Rex was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.680
hero Hourman. Rex and his wife were murdered&nbsp;
by Solomon Grundy, though Rick was told they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.760
died in a car crash. As a result, Rick grows&nbsp;
up angry, alienating everyone around him. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.880
Courtney Whitmore reveals to him that his father&nbsp;
had been Hourman and Beth Chapel shows him the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.640
truth of his death, he decides to turn his anger&nbsp;
on the Injustice Society. This anger makes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.560
undisciplined and sloppy. Eventually, he decides&nbsp;
to act for justice instead of revenge — however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.120
a lifetime of feeling abandoned still&nbsp;
makes anger his first response to stress.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:33.760
Yolanda Montez has great grades, popularity,&nbsp;
a likely win in the upcoming student election,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.040
and a boyfriend. When he pressures&nbsp;
her to send him a nude photo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.000
however, he shares it with everyone, humiliating&nbsp;
her in front of the whole school. Worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.240
her parents feel that she's disgraced&nbsp;
them, and stop taking her to church.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.600
It takes a persistent Courtney Whitmore to&nbsp;
convince her to become Wildcat and join her new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:57.600
Justice Society. Still, it takes Yolanda a long&nbsp;
time to work through her shame: For quite a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.880
she pushes everyone away. In time, she learns&nbsp;
to do things for the right reasons, but part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.920
her will always miss the life she once had. The&nbsp;
fact that she can never return to it haunts her.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:17.040
"When those photos got around, I&nbsp;
was ashamed to be Yolanda Montez."

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:23.120
Rene Ramirez starts his career as a vigilante&nbsp;
with sloppy working methods. Joining Team Arrow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.040
is an adjustment for everyone, because he&nbsp;
isn't used to working as part of a team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.720
and definitely isn't used to following orders. He&nbsp;
chafes at Oliver Queen's rigid leadership style,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:38.400
and constantly blows up. This makes him a major&nbsp;
liability. It isn't until much later that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.360
learns how to calm down and not take everything&nbsp;
so personally. His passion to do the right thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.760
is his greatest asset, but when that passion&nbsp;
boils over, he's a weak link in the field.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:54.000
John "Spartan" Diggle is a man who's constantly&nbsp;
trying to figure out his next step. He's been a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.840
soldier, a bodyguard, and eventually, a member of&nbsp;
Team Arrow. As important as he is to the cause, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.920
is always in Oliver's shadow. This dissatisfaction&nbsp;
eats at him, no matter how much he loves Oliver.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.360
Everything changes when Oliver decides to retire&nbsp;
for a while, leaving his role to Diggle. Being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.680
Green Arrow clearly means the world to&nbsp;
him, so when Oliver takes the role back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:21.840
Diggle is devastated. His need to be something&nbsp;
more than he is causes him to leave Team Arrow and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:27.200
move over to ARGUS — but that role doesn't suit&nbsp;
him either. It isn't until the end of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.840
which implies that he is chosen to be the&nbsp;
new Green Lantern, that he finds his place.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:37.920
Curtis Holt is an Olympic decathlete, a genius&nbsp;
engineer, and an academic, possessing 14 different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:43.360
degrees. Initially serving as part of Team Arrow's&nbsp;
support crew, he's beaten up by thugs and vows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:48.800
to never be put in that position again. He learns&nbsp;
hand-to-hand combat and becomes fairly good at it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:54.400
but never quite catches up to his teammates.&nbsp;
Moreover, PTSD often makes him hesitate in combat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.280
He later struggles with anger at Oliver Queen&nbsp;
for putting all new members under surveillance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.480
the dissolution of his marriage because of his&nbsp;
double life, and his distaste for ARGUS' tactics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.200
Eventually, Curtis quits the life, but remains&nbsp;
available for research and intelligence.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.560
Thea Queen starts out much like her brother:&nbsp;
A privileged partier who gets mixed up with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:19.920
lot of bad people. When she learns that Oliver's&nbsp;
arch-enemy Malcolm Merlyn is her actual father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.680
her life is upended. Merlyn trains her to become&nbsp;
a killer using League of Assassins methods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.800
She turns on him in time and becomes a member&nbsp;
of Team Arrow, but dies later on. She is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:36.560
revived by the Lazarus Pit, but it gives her an&nbsp;
insatiable bloodlust. Once she is cured of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:42.160
she takes a job in Oliver Queen's mayoral office&nbsp;
and makes some ethically dubious moves. No matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:48.320
what Thea does, she always goes too far, and&nbsp;
rarely considers the consequences of her actions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.480
Eventually, she retires from all kinds&nbsp;
of vigilante activity and public life.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:58.800
Roy Harper credits Oliver with giving him purpose&nbsp;
after a hard start in life. But poor Roy suffers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:03.680
as a result of becoming a crime-fighter, being&nbsp;
kidnapped and injected with serum that boosts his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:08.400
abilities at the cost of his mental stability.&nbsp;
While he eventually receives an antidote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:13.600
he is later killed and resurrected by the&nbsp;
bloodlust-inducing Lazarus Pit. He receives the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.720
special lotus formula to counteract this effect,&nbsp;
but the lingering influence of the serum continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:24.160
to urge him towards violence. Only by leaving&nbsp;
the vigilante life altogether can he control it.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:30.320
After gaining sonic powers, detective Dinah Drake&nbsp;
embarks upon a violent campaign of revenge on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.440
the criminals she believes killed her partner.&nbsp;
Eventually, Oliver Queen convinces her to join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.640
Team Arrow. She ultimately finds herself torn&nbsp;
between various allegiances — especially after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:46.080
discovering that the murderous Vigilante is in&nbsp;
fact her ex-partner and ex-boyfriend. She keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:52.320
this a secret, which is a major breach of trust.&nbsp;
Later, she, Mr. Terrific, and Wild Dog break away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:57.360
from Team Arrow after discovering they've been put&nbsp;
under surveillance. She is made chief of police,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.160
which puts her allegiance to the law-breaking&nbsp;
Team Arrow in jeopardy. Dinah is forced to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:07.840
betray the trust of either the police force, Team&nbsp;
Arrow, or both. When she travels to the future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:12.880
after Oliver Queen's funeral, she gives up the&nbsp;
adventurer's life for a long time as a result.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.240
Laurel Lance of Earth-2 wasn't lucky enough&nbsp;
to have a loving father around to raise her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:22.960
She drifts through life until she gains her&nbsp;
sonic scream, at which point she signs up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:28.000
Zoom to help him try to conquer Earth-1. She&nbsp;
causes further trouble assisting the likes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:33.760
Prometheus and Ricardo Diaz — but Quentin Lance,&nbsp;
Earth-1 Laurel's father, never gives up on her.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:38.160
Eventually, she becomes a force for good.&nbsp;
Her biggest flaw is her urge to ignore her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:42.960
newly-developed conscience — old habits die&nbsp;
hard, after all. Instead of blaming others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.400
she works hard to take her father's&nbsp;
love and faith in her to heart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.200
even though she is constantly&nbsp;
tempted to backslide.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.720
Ray Palmer is a genius, but perhaps more&nbsp;
importantly, he's the moral compass of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.080
Legends. But his kind and gentle nature can&nbsp;
be a liability. He's not a natural fighter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.360
and so he's not the guy who's going to battle&nbsp;
to his last breath to save the day. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:10.240
he prefers sitting down with his enemies, in the&nbsp;
hopes of persuading them to change their minds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.280
rather than fight them. This makes him a decent&nbsp;
person, but not always the best superhero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:20.400
His deciding to leave the group in order to&nbsp;
start a new life with Nora makes a lot of sense:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.480
As much as he enjoys hanging out with&nbsp;
his friends, he's not a lifelong soldier.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:30.080
Mick Rory becomes a criminal because he hates&nbsp;
authority. He also struggles with guilt over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.800
the death of his parents, who perished in&nbsp;
a blaze he set as a child. When he agrees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.360
to become a Legend, it's because he wants to&nbsp;
steal a bunch of stuff while time traveling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.040
While he betrays the team more than&nbsp;
once, he eventually settles back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:48.000
in as a cornerstone of the group — albeit,&nbsp;
one with a room full of stolen riches.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:52.640
After he changes a timeline and accidentally&nbsp;
fathers a daughter, Mick finds himself with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:57.680
mixed emotions. He doesn't want the responsibility&nbsp;
of fatherhood, but also doesn't want his daughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:01.920
to go through life without a dad. This&nbsp;
proves to be the one thing he can't ignore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:06.880
While he's warming to the role of parent, he&nbsp;
is wary of the responsibility he now shoulders.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:14.720
"C'mon, I'm trying. Alright, what is our&nbsp;
father-daughter weekend gonna look like?"

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:21.920
Ava Sharpe is recruited by Rip Hunter to work for&nbsp;
his Time Bureau, in order to protect the timeline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:27.040
with a rigid set of rules. She's all about&nbsp;
rigid rules, and loves her role in running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:32.720
the Bureau ... until she learns the horrible truth&nbsp;
about her past. She's a clone who had her memories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:37.680
wiped, which were replaced with fake ones. She&nbsp;
is later forced to fight clones of herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:42.400
which does a number on her identity. While she&nbsp;
finds a home with the Legends, and the love of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:47.920
her life, Sara Lance, Ava's still sensitive about&nbsp;
being a clone, and thus not a "real" person.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.600
"My, my life, my memories,&nbsp;
they're all manufactured.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:54.560
They're, they're not real. I'm not even real."

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:01.200
John Constantine pretends to be above it all. In&nbsp;
large part, this is because he's brought grief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:06.880
and pain to those around him. What's worse, his&nbsp;
guilt with regard to hard choices he's had to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.520
has led him to make even worse choices&nbsp;
in an effort to fix things. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:16.080
when he tries to alter the timeline to prevent&nbsp;
his boyfriend from being dragged off to Hell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:21.120
it just makes the ensuing timeline more&nbsp;
bizarre: Zari gets turned into a cat and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.680
the team is turned into puppets. Trying&nbsp;
to assuage his guilt on his own only makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:30.560
things worse for everyone, but it also makes&nbsp;
him even more afraid of relying on others.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:36.880
Whether it's Amaya Jiwe or her granddaughters&nbsp;
Mari and Kuasa filling the role, the heroine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:43.280
known as Vixen is always bound to defend Zambesi&nbsp;
Village with the Anansi Totem. Amaya does spend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:48.240
time away from her tribe as Vixen during World&nbsp;
War II when she joins the Justice Society,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:52.880
and then joins the time-spanning Legends.&nbsp;
But she knows that her time there is limited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.640
as she must return to Zambesi.&nbsp;
After the timeline is changed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:02.400
Mari and Kuasa decide to share the Anansi Totem,&nbsp;
growing up in solidarity, instead of as enemies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:07.120
However, no matter where they go or what they&nbsp;
do, their allegiance to their village and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.640
willingness to do whatever it takes to save it&nbsp;
makes this a permanent area of vulnerability.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.800
A shapeshifter, Charlie has a serious hatred&nbsp;
of authority and a general distrust of others.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:24.240
Eons ago, she was Clotho, one of the three&nbsp;
mythological Fates. She decided to break the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.640
loom that gave her and her sisters control&nbsp;
over mortal lives, however. She's been on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:34.080
the run from her sisters Atropos and Lachesis&nbsp;
ever since. Even when she's with the Legends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:39.840
she is guarded about her past, and doesn't trust&nbsp;
them enough to tell them her secrets. Coming clean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:43.920
might have prevented a lot of grief, as the&nbsp;
other two Fates eventually catch up with her.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:50.000
In many ways, Nora Darhk is the most unlikely&nbsp;
Legend of all. The daughter of their enemy Damien&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:55.200
Darhk, her parents died when they tried to destroy&nbsp;
most of the world in one of Damien's schemes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.200 --> 00:11:00.160
She is later connected to a cult and enslaved&nbsp;
by the demon Mallus in an effort to resurrect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:04.160
him. She is severely scarred and&nbsp;
traumatized by the experience.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:08.880
Despite all of this, Ray Palmer shows&nbsp;
her nothing but kindness, seeing only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:14.480
the good in her. When Damien sees this, he&nbsp;
sacrifices his own life to save his daughter's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.680
Nora's time as a Fairy Godmother allows her to&nbsp;
work through some of her childhood trauma, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:25.200
it takes embarking on a new life with Ray as his&nbsp;
wife and leaving the Legends behind to truly heal.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:30.640
Nate Heywood is a big, nerdy kid who gets&nbsp;
to use his knowledge of historical data to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:36.160
have the biggest adventure of his life. He loves&nbsp;
his friends and will do anything for them. Nate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:41.440
Ray, and Behrad form a sort of sub-fraternity&nbsp;
in the Legends, goofing around together and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:46.400
exchanging many high fives. But this endearing&nbsp;
quality of Nate's is also his weakness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:52.000
as he can be emotionally manipulated in the same&nbsp;
way a kid can. Not having a father who showed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:57.040
him love means that he searches constantly&nbsp;
for outside approval, and often makes poor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:02.320
decisions based on his feelings. Fortunately for&nbsp;
him, he has the Legends to keep him grounded.

00:12:03.536 --> 00:12:08.000
Mona Wu is sweet and naive. But that&nbsp;
niceness conceals a nasty, violent temper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:13.440
She doesn't just get angry — she has tantrums.&nbsp;
This impulsiveness is what gets her mixed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:17.760
with the Legends in the first place. When&nbsp;
she is scratched by a werewolf-like creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:22.320
called the Kaupe, she is transformed into&nbsp;
one herself. Suddenly, when she gets mad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:28.480
she turns into her "Wolfie" form and is perfectly&nbsp;
happy to attack both friends and foe alike. Anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:33.840
who triggers a tantrum is fair game, which makes&nbsp;
her more than a little unstable as a teammate.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:40.000
When the Legends change the timeline and Zari&nbsp;
Tomaz is replaced by her brother Behrad, it means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:45.440
that she suddenly disappeared into the Air Totem.&nbsp;
This is where the spirits of its former wielders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:51.360
live — but Zari the adventurer never existed in&nbsp;
the new timeline. Instead, there is Zari Tarazi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:56.880
the highly-pampered social media influencer.&nbsp;
This Zari accidentally discovers her brother is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:02.480
superhero and starts hanging out with the team. As&nbsp;
she learns about her other self and realizes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:08.000
flashes of her abilities have started to bubble&nbsp;
up in her, she stays with the Legends. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:13.040
she's still self-important, arrogant, and high&nbsp;
maintenance. She's just aggressive enough to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:16.560
away with it, but there are definitely&nbsp;
times she's tolerated more than loved.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:22.880
When the timeline is altered, Zari's brother&nbsp;
Behrad Tarazi becomes the Air Totem-bearing member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:27.520
of the Legends. On a team of slackers and&nbsp;
degenerates, Behrad still stands out as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:32.800
the most mellow member of the Legends, with a&nbsp;
supremely laid back personality. He's a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:38.800
too relaxed at times, in fact, as he doesn't&nbsp;
always take things as seriously as he needs to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:44.240
For him, these missions aren't life-and-death,&nbsp;
but a spirited adventure he's glad to be taking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:48.560
This attitude can be nice to be around,&nbsp;
but it also makes him hard to depend on.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:53.440
Leo Snart is a Freedom Fighter&nbsp;
from the Nazi-ruled Earth-X.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:58.640
After meeting the Legends, he decides to&nbsp;
briefly join the team and hang out on Earth-1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:04.800
Quite unlike his Earth-1 counterpart, this Leo&nbsp;
is meticulous and hates the Legends' sloppy ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:10.320
He particularly chastises Rory for using his&nbsp;
flamethrower indiscriminately. He doesn't stay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:15.600
with the Legends for very long, and though the&nbsp;
reasons why aren't related to his particular ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:20.480
he likely knows he's too fastidious to be&nbsp;
a long-term fit with this group of misfits.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:26.240
James Olsen is tired of feeling left out — that's&nbsp;
why he becomes the armored Guardian. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:32.800
after James is shot, Lena Luthor injects him with&nbsp;
the Kryptonian Harun-El serum. James gains actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:39.280
Kryptonian super-powers and loses control of them&nbsp;
when he struggles with PTSD-related panic attacks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:43.440
With professional help, he is able to&nbsp;
get through this, and in time, his system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:48.160
is purged of the serum. But the trauma of&nbsp;
the experiences, often triggered by hearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:52.960
gunshots or simply seeing Lex Luthor, is&nbsp;
something he will always have to manage.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:56.800
Nia takes up the mantle of&nbsp;
Dreamer after her mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.800 --> 00:15:02.480
the previous Dreamer, dies. Nia is an intense&nbsp;
perfectionist and her own worst critic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:08.320
This is exacerbated by her imperfect control&nbsp;
of her precognitive and dream-related powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:13.920
which leads her to misunderstand that her mother&nbsp;
is going to die. Nia has a lot to live up to as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:18.560
Dreamer, and she knows it, putting too much&nbsp;
pressure on herself as a result. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.600
she slowly overcomes this as she becomes&nbsp;
more confident and learns to ask for help.

00:15:24.617 --> 00:15:28.480
Mon-El and Kara are an unlikely&nbsp;
couple, but their bond is real.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:34.080
Tragically, they are separated when he is forced&nbsp;
to go to the 31st century for his own safety.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:39.200
There, he founds the Legion and marries fellow&nbsp;
member Imra. When they go back in time and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:44.240
finds himself face-to-face with Kara, he tries&nbsp;
to put her off, but it's not long before he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:49.280
realizes that he's still in love with her. This&nbsp;
starts to affect his judgment, his marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:55.440
and even the foundations of his heroism. He bases&nbsp;
too much of himself on her and eventually returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.440 --> 00:16:00.640
to the 31st century because he knows he has to,&nbsp;
putting the greater good above his own desires.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:07.200
J'onn J'onnz hates fire, which scares him so&nbsp;
badly, it affects his shapeshifting. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:12.320
what haunts him even more deeply is survivor's&nbsp;
guilt. He believes himself to be the last of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:17.120
the Green Martians, who were wiped out in a&nbsp;
genocide perpetrated by the White Martians.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:21.760
Even though he's since learned that his younger&nbsp;
brother and father are alive, J'onn never recovers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:26.640
from the death of his wife and children. He&nbsp;
still feels guilty for living while they cannot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:31.040
Enemies often exploit this chink in his&nbsp;
armor through the use of psychic attacks.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:37.520
Querl Dox is a tactical genius, an efficient&nbsp;
fighter, and an all-around powerhouse of digital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:43.600
might. However, he's wary of his ancestry, being&nbsp;
born into the Brainiac clan, descendants of one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:49.520
Superman's most relentless enemies. Kind-hearted&nbsp;
"Brainy" worries that evil lurks within him as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:54.560
well, and not without cause: He is cut off&nbsp;
from his emotions when his mind is rebooted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.560 --> 00:17:00.320
only regaining them and his sense of empathy when&nbsp;
he sees the love of his life, Nia Nal, in danger.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:05.840
Anissa Pierce is a brilliant young medical&nbsp;
student, part-time teacher, and community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:11.440
activist. Her strong ideals are backed up by her&nbsp;
courage and steely resolve. When she realizes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:16.240
she has superpowers, she keeps them hidden&nbsp;
so she can figure out what she is capable of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:22.320
in private. Still, she is reckless in attacking&nbsp;
the various gangs that plague Freeland. When her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:27.680
father finally gives her his blessing in exchange&nbsp;
for working as a team, she makes fewer mistakes in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:32.800
the field. Of course, she then concocts an&nbsp;
entirely new persona, Blackbird, that robs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:38.160
from gangs and gives money to the church and needy&nbsp;
people. She just can't help being a loose cannon.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:43.360
Jennifer Pierce never wanted superpowers,&nbsp;
but she gets them anyway. As she's not a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:48.720
natural fighter like her father and sister, she&nbsp;
tries to minimize their effect upon her life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:54.080
Her powers just can't be denied, however: When&nbsp;
she tries to not use them, they build up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.080 --> 00:18:00.240
cause her intense pain. Unlike Jefferson, who is&nbsp;
something of a battery, Jen is a generator. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:05.600
means that she can do pretty much anything her dad&nbsp;
can, but isn't at risk of running out of juice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:10.640
Accepting her powers comes slowly to her, but&nbsp;
fighting for her family makes it possible.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:17.520
Cisco Ramon is an integral part of Team Flash as&nbsp;
a hacker, leader, and tech guy. But being betrayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:22.960
by his mentor, who is actually the Reverse-Flash,&nbsp;
makes Cisco distrustful of everyone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:28.000
That even includes his best friend Barry Allen,&nbsp;
as he creates a weapon to stop him, just in case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:34.160
he turns evil, goes insane, or otherwise loses&nbsp;
control of his powers. This approach means Ramon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:39.120
is always a little on edge with everyone, even&nbsp;
as he projects an easygoing, friendly demeanor.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:43.200
After being introduced to the&nbsp;
nasty Killer Frost of Earth-2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:46.640
and realizing that her ex-lover&nbsp;
is actually the murderous Zoom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:51.840
Caitlin Snow slowly starts to feel her&nbsp;
long-dormant second personality emerge.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:57.120
When her other side takes over, she is every bit&nbsp;
as vicious as her Earth-2 counterpart. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:02.640
the love shown to her by members of Team Flash&nbsp;
allows both Caitlin and Killer Frost to co-exist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:08.240
taking turns "driving." Still, this relationship&nbsp;
with her other self has its ups and downs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:11.600
When her two sides quarrel or don't&nbsp;
feel they're getting enough time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:14.480
"driving," Caitlin gets&nbsp;
more than a little unstable.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:19.280
When Ralph Dibny first receives his&nbsp;
powers, he's a private detective.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:24.480
He works as a PI because he was disgraced&nbsp;
as a cop, having planted false evidence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:28.960
When he becomes a hero and starts taking&nbsp;
Barry Allen's lessons and example to heart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:32.640
he legitimately changes his ways&nbsp;
and stops cutting moral corners.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:37.040
"I don't do that kind of stuff&nbsp;
anymore. Ralph Dibny's gone straight."

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:41.120
"You serious?" I got friends&nbsp;
now. They're good people."

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:46.800
However, Ralph's icky personality endures&nbsp;
— especially when it comes to dealing with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:52.560
women. His romantic "advice" to others is like&nbsp;
something out of a pick-up artist handbook.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:58.320
What's more, even as Ralph has gained humility&nbsp;
in many ways, he still sees himself as a font of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:02.800
wisdom. He's just too in love with his own&nbsp;
patter to take a hard look in the mirror.

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:09.440
Wally West is one of the most unsettled heroes in&nbsp;
the Arrowverse. Having grown up in dysfunctional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:14.560
circumstances, he struggles with tension and&nbsp;
jealousy. When he gains his own super speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:19.200
he is reckless and a bit of a glory hog.&nbsp;
He is so overjoyed to have superpowers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:22.560
in fact, that he starts to use&nbsp;
them for the wrong reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:27.680
Though he eventually comes to terms with his&nbsp;
anger and jealousy, he leaves Central City — he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:33.040
just never manages to feel like he fits in. He&nbsp;
goes off to find himself in a Buddhist monastery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:38.560
and is later convinced to join the Legends. Wally&nbsp;
makes some friends, but eventually quits that too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:43.280
Kid Flash could be an all-star superhero,&nbsp;
but his lack of direction holds him back.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:49.760
In many ways, Kate Kane is a better superhero&nbsp;
than her cousin, Bruce Wayne: She's more flexible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:54.400
in her thinking and more willing to ask for&nbsp;
help. Furthermore, she is a steadying force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:54.400 --> 00:21:00.000
when she becomes the paragon of courage during the&nbsp;
Crisis. However, the return of her seemingly dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:06.160
twin sister Beth as the psychotic criminal Alice&nbsp;
repeatedly leads Batwoman to make major mistakes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:11.200
Kate captures and lets her go on more than&nbsp;
one occasion, despite her homicidal ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:16.080
The survivor's guilt Kate feels over the fact&nbsp;
that she stopped looking for Beth years earlier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:21.520
is simply more than she can bear. As a result,&nbsp;
more than one person she cares about is murdered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:26.160
and Kate has to deal with knowing that they'd&nbsp;
likely be alive if she'd had more resolve.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:32.160
As you likely know, Superman's biggest physical&nbsp;
weakness is green kryptonite, which is lethal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:37.520
in large enough doses. Furthermore, red kryptonite&nbsp;
turns him evil and silver kryptonite makes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:42.960
hallucinate. He's also vulnerable to magic&nbsp;
and mind control. However, his real weakness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:48.240
is the love of his life, Lois Lane, and his&nbsp;
adoptive parents, Martha and Jonathan Kent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:52.480
He's terrified of enemies learning about them,&nbsp;
and now he's frightened that something will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:56.320
happen to his new baby. This doesn't&nbsp;
stop him from doing the right thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:56.320 --> 00:22:01.200
but enemies who know anything about him know to&nbsp;
strike at him through his family. Lex Luthor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:04.240
his arch-enemy, knows this most keenly of all.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:10.000
When Courtney Whitmore discovers the cosmic&nbsp;
staff among her stepfather's belongings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:14.320
everything changes. The staff allows&nbsp;
her to bond with it to become Stargirl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:18.800
and she sets about forming a new Justice&nbsp;
Society. Despite her stepfather's warnings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:23.280
over-eager Courtney makes a lot of mistakes&nbsp;
with her recklessness, even getting people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:27.600
killed. She thinks that having powers and&nbsp;
her own team will somehow solve everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:31.920
without considering that the original&nbsp;
Justice Society also had their own powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:36.240
and were still murdered by their enemies.&nbsp;
While she eventually calms down a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:41.040
with regard to leading the new JSA, she still&nbsp;
tends to act without thinking things through.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:46.160
Jefferson Pierce's paternalistic attitude&nbsp;
doesn't just affect his family, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:51.200
people he works with as well. In thinking&nbsp;
he knows how to protect everyone best,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:56.640
he often makes unilateral decisions that don't&nbsp;
respect the agency of his super-powered daughters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:56.640 --> 00:23:02.240
his highly capable wife, his students, and even&nbsp;
his allies in the Freeland Police Department.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:06.960
It takes him a long time to figure out that&nbsp;
people are going to do what they want to do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:12.880
and that he has to cooperate. The irony of this&nbsp;
is that as a school principal, his whole job is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:18.160
trying to find ways to empower young people.&nbsp;
As a superhero, he doesn't do that enough.

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:24.000
Sara Lance starts off as a party girl who has&nbsp;
an affair with her sister Laurel's boyfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:29.440
Oliver Queen. After their ill-fated yacht trip,&nbsp;
she does what she has to do to survive: She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:35.680
helps torture people aboard the Amazo, joins the&nbsp;
League of Assassins, and becomes a trained killer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:41.600
Eventually, she breaks away to become a vigilante.&nbsp;
Though she dies, she is resurrected — but her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:47.040
reanimated body lacks a soul, which leads to&nbsp;
her becoming a killing machine. Even when her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:52.000
soul is reunited with her body, she is haunted&nbsp;
by the rage inside of her that she often can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:57.120
control. Nora Darhk is eventually able to help&nbsp;
her with this, but it doesn't erase her past.

00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:04.000
Of all the heroes in the Arrowverse, Kara Danvers&nbsp;
is surely the nicest. She's a kind, compassionate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:09.520
and loving person who works well on her own and&nbsp;
as part of a larger team. She's also willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:14.720
to see the good in nearly everyone, which can&nbsp;
be a liability. You can't blame her too much:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:18.800
How would you handle birth parents who&nbsp;
invent horrifying technology designed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:24.320
to murder and/or enslave people? Her adoptive&nbsp;
father, Jeremiah Danvers, isn't much better:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:24.320 --> 00:24:30.240
He's a double agent who uses Kara's trusting&nbsp;
nature to hide his betrayal. Her naivete has faded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:30.240 --> 00:24:35.440
after these experiences, and she's become more&nbsp;
battle-hardened and confident. But she's still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:35.440 --> 00:24:41.040
the paragon of hope, and while that's very much a&nbsp;
strength, this optimism is often used against her.

00:24:41.840 --> 00:24:46.960
Barry Allen's inherent decency is his greatest&nbsp;
strength: It makes him a wonderful friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:52.560
a great team member, and a stalwart hero. However,&nbsp;
once Barry makes up his mind about something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:58.000
it's impossible to get him to change course.&nbsp;
He'd rather learn by catastrophic example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:02.800
than accept the wisdom of others. That's&nbsp;
especially true if the stakes are personal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:02.800 --> 00:25:08.080
The trauma of seeing his parents killed unhinges&nbsp;
him to the point where he alters the timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:08.080 --> 00:25:13.200
inadvertently changing the lives of everyone&nbsp;
he loves ... and not always for the better.

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:17.680
He frantically tries to fix this mess,&nbsp;
but things never quite return to normal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:23.200
It takes Earth-2's Flash, Jay Garrick, to&nbsp;
teach him that he simply has to let it go.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:28.320
Barry mostly avoids mucking with the timeline&nbsp;
following this crisis, but not entirely.

00:25:29.120 --> 00:25:33.360
Oliver Queen thinks that he knows best for&nbsp;
everyone, and rarely deviates from acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:38.640
on this belief. He is enormously distrustful,&nbsp;
conceals secrets, and openly lies in the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:38.640 --> 00:25:44.080
of protecting his loved ones. This alienates&nbsp;
much of Team Arrow, and nearly destroys his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:50.480
relationship with Felicity Smoak. Admittedly, his&nbsp;
unilateral decision-making does save the universe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:50.480 --> 00:25:54.480
Oliver sacrifices himself in order&nbsp;
to create the new Earth-Prime and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:54.480 --> 00:25:59.360
resurrects billions of lives. It's almost&nbsp;
as though he knows his form of leadership&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:59.360 --> 00:26:03.840
is no longer viable in this new world. He&nbsp;
can't change his domineering ways ... and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:03.840 --> 00:26:08.000
so he makes one final, sweeping choice&nbsp;
that takes him out of the equation.

00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:11.280
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:11.280 --> 00:26:14.480
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite Arrowverse characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:14.480 --> 00:26:23.840
are coming soon. Subscribe to our YouTube channel&nbsp;
and hit the bell so you don't miss a single one.

